# Line endings must be deterministic on every platform. Git for Windows installs
# with core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites detected-text files LF -> CRLF on
# checkout: that turned bin/codeatlas-viewer's `#!/bin/sh` into `#!/bin/sh^M`, so
# a Windows user's very first command died with "bad interpreter". Pin both
# directions rather than trusting the client's config.
* text=auto eol=lf

# ...except the Windows shims, which cmd.exe wants with CRLF.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf

# Never touch binaries.
*.png binary
*.sqlite binary
